$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(3):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a three necked flask, 2-bromoaniline (5, 0.86 g, 5.0 mmol),
benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-ylboronic acid (4, 1.08 g, 6.5 mmol), Na2CO3 (1.33
g, 12.5 mmol) and 25 mL of solvent (toluene/EtOH/H2O= 1:1:1) were added.
Then, Pd(PPh3)4 (0.29 g, 0.25 mmol) was added and the mixture was stirred
for 4 h at 80 °C under N2. After completion, the mixture was cooled to
room temperature, quenched with saturated NH4Cl and extracted with EtOAc.
The organic layer was washed with saturated NaCl and dried over MgSO4.
After removing the volatiles in vacuo, the residue was subjected to
column chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate =
20:1). 2-(benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)aniline as a brown oil (6, 0.91 g,
85%).
