$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM β,meso-Dimer 19. Porphyrin 16b (96 mg, 0.100 mmol), porphyrin 14e (105
mg, 0.125 mmol), and Ba(OH)2 (315 mg, 1.0 mmol) were dissolved in toluene
(100 mL) and water (20 mL) and degassed with an argon stream in an
ultrasonic bath for 15 min. Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mg, 0.01 mmol) was added and
the mixture degassed for further 20 min. Then the reaction mixture was
heated to 110 °C for 6 h. After it was cooled to room temperature, the
organic phase was filtered over a plug of silica and fully eluted with
ethyl acetate. After evaporation of all solvents, the residue was
purified by column chromatography (silica, n-hexane/dichloromethane 2/1 →
0/1). 125 mg, 78% yield. Mp >300 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ -2.66 (s,
2H), -2.30 (s, 2H), -1.14 (s, 9H), -0.10 (s, 6H), 0.24 (s, 6H), 1.37 (s,
9H), 1.58 (s, 9H), 1.67 (s, 9H), 3.63 (d, 3 J = 10.1 Hz, 2H), 3.70 (d, 3
J = 10.1 Hz, 2H), 5.19 (d, 3 J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 6.63 (dd, 3 J = 8.3 Hz, 4 J
= 2.2 Hz, 2H), 6.96 (d, 3 J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.47-7.57 (m, 4H), 7.68 (d, 3
J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.73 (d, 3 J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.84 (d, 3 J = 7.8 Hz 2H),
8.15 (d, 3 J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 8.26 (d, 3 J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 8.37 (d, 3 J =
4.9 Hz, 1H), 8.39 (d, 3 J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 8.47 (d, 3 J = 4.7 Hz, 2H), 8.48
(d, 3 J = 4.7 Hz, 2H), 8.69 (d, 3 J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 8.84 (d, 3 J = 4.6 Hz,
2H), 8.90-8.97 (m, 4H), 9.02 (d, 3 J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 9.06 (d, 3 J = 4.8
Hz, 1H), 9.09 (d, 3 J = 4.6 Hz, 2H), 9.60 (s, 1H), 9.80 (s, 1H) ppm. 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 158.7, 150.7, 150.6, 150.4, 147.4, 139.8, 139.4,
139.3, 136.4, 134.8, 134.8, 134.6, 133.0, 132.0, 131.0, 131.0, 130.5,
129.8, 129.2, 128.4, 127.8, 123.9, 123.7, 123.6, 122.5, 120.6, 120.5,
120.3, 119.4, 113.9, 110.7, 102.9, 63.6, 53.6, 35.1, 35.0, 34.9, 32.1,
31.9, 31.9, 31.8, 31.7, 29.9, 28.8, 13.7, 13.3. MS (MALDI): m/z 1204.738
[M]•+. MS (MALDI): m/z 1488.759 [M]•+. HRMS (ESI): calcd for C104H97N8O2
[M + H]+ 1489.77290, found 1489.77454.
