$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the synthesis of Pyridone Ik and Il Pyridone of
general structure D (0.49 mmol), Benzo[b]thien-3-ylboronic acid
(0.99mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (0.024 mmol), and KF (0.99 mmol) were dissolved
in MeOH (4.0 mL), and the reaction heated by MWI at 140 °C for 10 min.
The reaction mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was
washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated.
Purification by column chromatography eluting with (Heptane:ethyl acetate
1:1→1:9) gave desired compound. Methyl
(3R)-7-cyclopropyl-4-oxo-6-{(7-thiabicyclo[4.3.0]nona-1,3,5,8-tetraen-9-yl)methyl}-1-thia-3a-aza-3-indancarboxylate(Ik):
Prepared by following the general procedure, white foam 291mg (70%).
[α]D-54 (c 1.2, CHCl3); IR ν 1753, 1655, 1579, 1490, 1428, 1356, 1212,
729 cm-1; 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.64-0.68 (m, 2H), 0.82-0.90 (m, 2H),
1.50-1.55 (m, 1H), 3.49 (dd, J = 2.4, 11.6 Hz, 1H), 3.65 (dd, J = 8.4,
11.6 Hz, 1H), 3.79 (s, 3H), 4.23 (q, J = 26.4 Hz, 2H), 5.58 (dd, J = 2.4,
8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.02 (s, 1H), 7.08 (s, 1H), 7.32-7.37 (m, 2H), 7.63-7.66 (m,
1H), 7.83-7.87 (m, 1H); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.5, 7.8, 11.1, 31.7,
32.3, 53.3, 62.8, 113.6, 115.4, 121.7, 123.0, 124.0, 124.2, 124.5, 132.6,
138.6, 140.6, 147.4, 155.5, 161.3, 168.7. LCMS m/z = 398 (M+H),
C21H19NO3S2 requires 397.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
